  "question": "Background / Context:\n\nThe project involves the development of a predictive analytics system for the San Francisco Department of Public Health. The system will manage data about food-related businesses, inspections, and violations. This involves predicting unscheduled inspection scores to ensure public health standards are maintained across eateries.\n\nObjectives:\n\n1. Predict inspection scores for unscheduled inspections from 2013 to 2016, with scores ranging from 1 to 100.\n2. Use historical data to enhance the Department's ability to forecast potential public health risks.\n\nStakeholders & Users:\n\n- San Francisco Department of Public Health officials\n- Data analysts and public health inspectors\n- Business owners affected by inspections\n\nFunctional Descriptions:\n\n1. Business Management:\n   - Store and manage data on businesses, including identification, location, and ownership details.\n   \n2. Inspection Record Keeping:\n   - Maintain a log of inspections, including scores, dates, and types.\n   - Facilitate the prediction of future inspection scores based on historical inspection data.\n\n3. Violation Tracking:\n   - Document violations, including type and risk category.\n   - Link violations to businesses and specific inspection events.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions:\n\n- The system should ensure the confidentiality and integrity of business data.\n- Data processing should be efficient to allow timely predictions and analysis.\n- The solution must scale to handle a large volume of data spanning several years of records.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0128\nCREATE TABLE `businesses` (\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `business_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `zip_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(30) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(10,7) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(10,7) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`business_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `inspections` (\n  `inspection_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `inspection_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `inspection_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `inspection_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`inspection_id`),\n  KEY `business_id` (`business_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inspections_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`business_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `violations` (\n  `violation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `inspection_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `violation_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `risk_category` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `violation_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`violation_id`),\n  KEY `inspection_id` (`inspection_id`),\n  KEY `business_id` (`business_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `violations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`inspection_id`) REFERENCES `inspections` (`inspection_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `violations_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`business_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
